---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Arrow from '../../../components/Arrow.astro';
import DisclosureIcon from '../../../components/DisclosureIcon.astro';
import MediaPlayer from '../../../components/MediaPlayer.astro';
import {nevermore, hasMedia, url, media} from '../../../lib/catalogue';
const release = nevermore.candidate!;
const file = nevermore.download!;
const megabytes = Math.round(file.bytes / 1024 / 1024);
const modes=[
  {name:'SOFT', kicker:'Magical Halloween', text:'The original haunting. Meet the Midnight Host, choose Trick or Treat, then let twenty encounters find you: ravens, ghosts, a spider and a few gentle surprises.'},
  {name:'HAUNTED', kicker:'Supernatural horror', text:'A cinematic haunting for those who want the dark. Rarer, stranger encounters, outcomes that answer your choices, and discoveries you will have to earn. Some of it is best left unseen until it finds you.'},
];
const moments=[
  {image:'host.webp', title:'Meet the Midnight Host.', text:'A figure emerges. A hand invites you closer. “Trick or Treat?” Your choice matters. What happens next is still a surprise.',alt:'The Skull Warden, Nevermore’s Midnight Host, extends an open hand.'},
  {image:'raven.webp', title:'Something heard you.', text:'Say “Raven” while armed and idle. A sweep, a watchful perch, perhaps something closer. The same word does not always bring the same encounter.',alt:'Azure Night raven in flight with detailed charcoal and cool-blue feathers.'},
  {image:'bride.webp', title:'Not everything is a scare.', text:'A spectral bride releases a butterfly. A chest offers a treat. Between the unsettling moments, there is room for something beautiful.',alt:'The Veiled Wraith Bride releases a butterfly from her open palm.'},
];
---
<Layout title="Nevermore — Halloween for AR Smart Glasses | GlassPlay" description="Nevermore Halloween 1.1.0: one application, two modes. Choose SOFT for magical Halloween surprises or HAUNTED for supernatural horror. Free download for Windows and Raven Simulator." path="experiences/nevermore/" theme="nevermore" social={hasMedia ? 'media/nevermore/glassplay-social.webp' : 'brand/nevermore-social.png'}>
  <section class="nevermore-hero wrap" aria-labelledby="nevermore-title">
    <a class="back-link" href={url('#experiences')}><span class="back-arrow"><Arrow /></span>GlassPlay experiences</a>
    <div class="nevermore-title"><h1 id="nevermore-title">{nevermore.name}</h1><span>{nevermore.theme} · Version {release.version}</span></div>
    <div class:list={['nevermore-hero-frame', {'title-art-frame':!hasMedia}]}>
      <img src={hasMedia ? media('cover.webp') : url('brand/nevermore-poster.webp')} srcset={hasMedia ? `${media('cover-small.webp')} 640w, ${media('cover.webp')} 1200w` : `${url('brand/nevermore-poster-small.webp')} 800w, ${url('brand/nevermore-poster.webp')} 1600w`} sizes="(max-width: 760px) 95vw, 90vw" alt={hasMedia ? 'Azure Night raven sweeps into the foreground, with the Midnight Host and Spectral Bride emerging behind it. A composition of approved production frames.' : 'Original 3D title artwork: a dark feather with restrained blue highlights.'} width={hasMedia ? '1200' : '1600'} height={hasMedia ? '630' : '1000'} fetchpriority="high" />
      <div class="hero-statement"><p>You armed something.<br /><em>Now it's here.</em></p><a class="button pale" href="#get-nevermore">Get Nevermore<Arrow /></a></div>
    </div>
    {!hasMedia && <p class="caption">Original title artwork.</p>}
  </section>

  <section class="story-intro wrap">
    <h2>Silence.<br />Presence.<br /><em>Then, an encounter.</em></h2>
    <div><p class="large-copy">Nevermore Halloween {release.version}.<br />One application. Two modes.</p><p>Arm Nevermore and go on looking at your world. A pair of eyes. A shadow. A raven passing too close. Encounters arrive with space between them, so anticipation has time to grow.</p><p>Some ask you to choose. Some simply arrive. You decide when it all ends.</p></div>
  </section>

  <section class="modes-section wrap" id="modes" aria-labelledby="modes-heading">
    <div class="section-intro"><h2 id="modes-heading">Two doors.<br /><em>Choose your night.</em></h2><p><strong>The Threshold</strong> is where every session begins. Look at a door and hold your gaze: it wakes, swings open on its hinges, and stepping through arms that mode. Click or use the keyboard if you prefer. DISARM walks you back through.</p></div>
    <div class="modes">{modes.map(mode=><article><h3>{mode.name}<span class="small-label">{mode.kicker}</span></h3><p>{mode.text}</p></article>)}</div>
  </section>

  <section class="film-section wrap" id="film" aria-labelledby="film-heading">
    <div class="section-intro"><h2 id="film-heading">A glimpse<br /><em>after dark.</em></h2><p>{hasMedia ? 'A short teaser: real production animation and a Windows capture in Raven Simulator Room. Play with sound. It is a glimpse, not a tour of everything SOFT and HAUNTED hold.' : 'Discover the atmosphere and the encounters.'}</p></div>
    <MediaPlayer />
    {hasMedia && <details class="film-description"><summary>Read the film description<DisclosureIcon /></summary><p>The Azure Night raven flies close. The Midnight Host emerges from black, inviting a choice with “Trick or Treat?” A Mimic Chest opens, and the Spectral Bride releases a butterfly. Labelled Room sections show translucent encounters over a simulated kitchen. Cloth, wing sounds and the raven call accompany the action. This is an edited teaser montage of encounters, not a continuous play session, not a demonstration of all of HAUNTED, and not footage from physical glasses.</p><a href={media('transcript.md')}>Read the complete transcript</a></details>}
  </section>

  <section class="moments wrap" aria-label="Nevermore encounters">
    {moments.map((moment,index)=><article class:list={['moment',{'reverse':index%2===1}]}>
      {hasMedia ? <img src={media(moment.image)} srcset={`${media(moment.image.replace('.webp','-small.webp'))} 480w, ${media(moment.image)} 960w`} sizes="(max-width:760px) 90vw, 50vw" alt={moment.alt} width="960" height="720" loading="lazy" /> : <div class:list={['moment-title-art',`moment-art-${index}`]} aria-hidden="true"><span>{index===0 ? 'Trick\nor Treat?' : index===1 ? '“Raven.”' : 'A strange\nkind of beautiful.'}</span></div>}
      <div><h2>{moment.title}</h2><p>{moment.text}</p>{index===1 && <p class="small-copy">Local voice recognition works in both modes on Windows and Raven Simulator. Physical Prism microphone behaviour is unverified.</p>}</div>
    </article>)}
  </section>

  <section class="ritual-section wrap" aria-labelledby="ritual-heading">
    <div class="section-intro"><h2 id="ritual-heading">An invitation.<br /><em>Never an obligation.</em></h2><p>No constant attention required. Nevermore leaves room for the real world, and always leaves you in control.</p></div>
    <ol class="ritual">
      <li><span class="ritual-number">1</span><h3>Choose a door.</h3><p>SOFT or HAUNTED. Nothing starts until you walk through and invite it in.</p></li>
      <li><span class="ritual-number">2</span><h3>Trick or Treat?</h3><p>Meet the Host. Choose, encounter, then return to silence.</p></li>
      <li><span class="ritual-number">3</span><h3>Call the raven.</h3><p>Say “Raven” while idle. Encounters respect pacing and cooldowns.</p></li>
      <li><span class="ritual-number">4</span><h3>Disarm. Instantly.</h3><p>Stop the video, audio and pending encounters. Your world is yours again.</p></li>
    </ol>
    <div class="privacy-note"><h3>A haunting that stays with you.</h3><p>Encounters and voice recognition run locally. Listening is limited to the armed, idle experience. Normal operation does not retain microphone recordings. Discoveries are saved on your device.</p></div>
  </section>

  <section class="availability wrap" id="get-nevermore" aria-labelledby="availability-heading">
    <div><h2 id="availability-heading">Your first encounter<br /><em>is waiting.</em></h2><p>Nevermore Halloween {release.version} brings SOFT and HAUNTED together in one free download, verified on Windows with Raven Simulator. It needs Python and Raven Framework, which you obtain separately.</p><a class="button" href={nevermore.install_url!}>Download Nevermore {release.version}<Arrow /></a><dl class="download-facts"><div><dt>File</dt><dd>{file.file} · about {megabytes} MB</dd></div><div><dt>SHA-256</dt><dd><code>{file.sha256}</code></dd></div><div><dt>Release</dt><dd><a href={nevermore.release_url!}>Release notes and checksum file</a></dd></div></dl><p class="small-copy">No sign-up or account required by the experience.</p><a class="text-link creator-link" href="https://github.com/RBraga01">Meet the creator <Arrow /></a></div>
    <div class="compatibility"><h3>Where it runs</h3><dl>{nevermore.targets.map(target=><div><dt>{target.name}</dt><dd>{target.label}</dd></div>)}</dl><p class="small-copy">Simulator footage shows a software preview. It does not establish the display, speaker, microphone, performance or thermals of physical glasses.</p></div>
    <div class="technical-details">
      <details><summary>Requirements & installation<DisclosureIcon /></summary><div><p>Nevermore is a Python application package, not a standalone executable. It requires Windows, Python 3.10 or later and Raven Framework 1.0.6, which is <strong>not included</strong>: obtain and use it separately under Raven Resonance's applicable terms. No SDK, app IDs, keys or credentials are included. A microphone is needed only for the optional “Raven” interaction.</p><ol class="install-steps"><li>Check the download: in PowerShell, <code>Get-FileHash {file.file} -Algorithm SHA256</code> must match the SHA-256 above.</li><li>Extract the ZIP and open PowerShell in the <code>Nevermore-Halloween</code> folder.</li><li>Create an environment with <code>python -m venv .venv</code> and activate it with <code>.venv/Scripts/Activate.ps1</code>.</li><li>Install your authorized Raven Framework 1.0.6 with <code>python -m pip install -e &lt;path-to-raven-framework&gt;</code>.</li><li>Run <code>python -m pip install -r requirements.txt</code>, then <code>python main.py</code>. The Threshold opens with both doors.</li></ol><p>The ZIP's <code>README.md</code>, <code>docs/installation.md</code> and <code>RAVEN_FRAMEWORK.md</code> have the full steps; <code>python tools/verify_release.py</code> checks every file after extraction.</p></div></details>
      <details><summary>Comfort & known limitations<DisclosureIcon /></summary><div><p>Nevermore contains sudden appearances, spiders and close creature encounters. Arm it intentionally, use a comfortable volume, and DISARM whenever you wish. Avoid use where distraction could be unsafe.</p><p>Prism uses an additive display: black contributes no light. Very bright real-world backgrounds can wash out dark detail. Room is the practical Simulator reference. Physical Prism is DEVICE-UNVERIFIED, and this is not an official Prism installation.</p><p>Local keyword detection depends on the microphone and surroundings; a voice invocation may be ignored during playback or cooldown. Speech recognition on physical Prism has not been verified.</p></div></details>
      <details><summary>Credits & licensing<DisclosureIcon /></summary><div><p>Nevermore brings together character artwork created with Meshy, animation authored for the experience, recorded Foley and generated character voices. Only finished rendered visuals are presented; original source models are not distributed.</p><p>Nevermore code is MIT-licensed. Nevermore-specific artwork and media are All Rights Reserved. Third-party materials keep their own licenses, listed in the ZIP's <code>THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md</code> and <code>CREDITS.json</code>. Raven Framework is a separate dependency, not included or relicensed.</p><a href={url('credits/#nevermore')}>Read credits and release information</a></div></details>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
